.TH PELOAD 1 "August 2026" "vst-ace" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
peload \- load and render an audio plug\-in from the command line, without Wine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peload
.RI { plugin | bank.json }
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B peload
loads a plug\-in built for Windows, macOS or Linux and runs it as native code
on Linux. It reports what the file is, lists its programs and parameters,
applies a patch, renders audio to a WAV, and can open the plug\-in's own editor
and capture it.
.PP
The loader is chosen from the file itself unless
.B \-\-as
overrides it. A bank names the plug\-in it was written for, so
.B peload
.I bank.json
opens that plug\-in with the patch already applied.
.PP
Plug\-ins are hosted out of process by default, through the
.B peserve
helper beside this program.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-detect
Say what platform and loader the file needs, then stop.
.TP
.B \-\-params
List every exposed parameter with its value.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-programs
Name the plug\-in's own programs.
.TP
.B \-\-render " \fIout.wav\fR"
Render to a WAV.
.B \-\-secs,
.B \-\-note,
.B \-\-program
and
.B \-\-block
control what is rendered and in what block size.
.TP
.B \-\-patch " \fIbank.json\fR"
Apply a patch before rendering.
.B \-\-pick
selects one when the file holds several, and
.B \-\-list\-patches
names them.
.TP
.B \-\-save\-patch " \fIout.json\fR"
Write the current state as a patch.
.TP
.B \-\-editor " \fIout.ppm\fR"
Open the plug\-in's GUI and capture it.
.TP
.B \-\-as " \fIkind\fR"
Force a loader instead of auto\-detecting: \fBauto\fR, \fBwin\-vst2\-64\fR,
\fBwin\-vst2\-32\fR, \fBwin\-vst3\fR, \fBlinux\-vst3\fR, \fBlinux\-vst2\fR,
\fBmac\-vst2\fR, \fBmac\-vst3\fR, \fBmac\-au\fR or \fBclassic\-mac\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PELOAD_DLL_PATH
Colon\-separated directories to search for a Windows runtime DLL a plug\-in
needs at load time.
.TP
.BR PESERVE ", " PELOAD32
Override the paths to the helper programs, found in
.I /usr/lib/vst\-ace
otherwise.
.TP
.B PEHOST_ISOLATE
Set to 0 to host in process rather than behind the helper.
.TP
.B PELOAD_VERBOSE
Report loading in detail.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dw (1),
.BR pestudio (1),
.BR dwstudio (1).
